  "cat:Sunset Hike in Tyresta National Park\nExplore the real Sweden, its nature and wildlife on a guided sunset hike through Tyresta National Park. Experience ancient forests with still lakes and pine trees that are hundreds of years old. You meet late in the day in central Stockholm and go together out into the wilderness. The dusk and darkness is the best time to encounter wild animals like deer and wild bores.": {
    "value": "sports",
    "fetchedAt": 1788794996440
  },
  "cat:Guided Hike in Stockholm Nature Reserve + Campfire Lunch\nTake a break from the hustle and bustle of Stockholm and immerse yourself in the serene surroundings of the Nacka Nature Reserve. Just a quick 20-minute drive from the city, this beautiful reserve is the perfect place to spend a day in nature. Enjoy a leisurely walk through the dense forests and over the high granite cliffs, taking in the views and fresh air. You will also be treated to a campfire-cooked lunch, adding an authentic touch to your experience.": {
    "value": "sports",
    "fetchedAt": 1788794996440
  },
  "cat:Evening tour along quays and Skeppsholmen\nEnjoy an evening walk through central Stockholm along waterfronts, parks and historic quays. Passing landmarks such as the Royal Dramatic Theatre, the National Museum, the Royal Palace and the Opera, you will discover the city&#x27;s history, architecture and maritime heritage, including beautiful Skeppsholmen. The tour ends in Kungsträdgården, close to restaurants and cafés.": {
    "value": "other",
    "fetchedAt": 1788794996440
  },
  "cat:Slussen, Old Djurgårdsstaden & the Vasa Museum\nFrom Slussen to Djurgården, discover Stockholm&#x27;s maritime history and urban development. The walk begins where Lake Mälaren meets the Baltic Sea and continues to the historic wooden houses of Djurgårdsstaden. The tour ends with admission and a guided visit to the Vasa Museum, home to the famous warship that sank in 1628 and was salvaged more than 300 years later.": {
    "value": "art",
    "fetchedAt": 1788794996440
  },
  "cat:Södermalm's heights - city walk with a view\nJoin on a walk through Södermalm&#x27;s historic heights, from Slussen to Medborgarplatsen. Strolling along Glasbruksgatan, Fiskargatan and Mosebacke, enjoy beautiful views and discover stories of people, places and transformation. Learn how Södermalm evolved from a working-class district into one of Stockholm&#x27;s most creative and vibrant neighbourhoods.": {
    "value": "other",
    "fetchedAt": 1788794996440
  },
  "cat:Daily Stockholm bike tour\nExperience Stockholm in a different way, on a comfortable bike with spectacular views. We pass the most iconic areas at a relaxed pace and take a nice break in the middle of the tour. This experience is for people from all over the world and also for &#x27;Stockholmers&#x27;. A special Swedish-Dutch history tour is also offered. Tours are given at 9.30 and 13.30 every day.": {
    "value": "sports",
    "fetchedAt": 1788794996440
  },
  "cat:Old Town Sightseeing Tour\nOld town, or “Gamla stan” as it is known locally, is by far the most mythical and legendary neighbourhood in all of Stockholm. As the citys historical center, this is where you find out about ancient events and hear fascinating stories and tales that will last for a lifetime! With this tour its like you step in to a time machine and are whisked back to the to middle ages where noblemen, princesses and dukes roamed the streets.": {
    "value": "other",
    "fetchedAt": 1788794996440
  },
  "cat:From the City Hall tower to the silhouette of Storkyrkan\nDiscover central Stockholm on a guided walk including admission to Stockholm City Hall and Stockholm Cathedral. Explore the magnificent halls of City Hall, home of the Nobel Banquet, and visit the city&#x27;s cathedral with its royal history, the famous Sun Dog Painting and St. George and the Dragon. The tour ends at the Royal Palace with the chance to see the changing of the guard.": {
